---
<p>Bayan looks like Python with the types written in: short lines, no ceremony, a <code>for</code> loop over anything. But types are checked before the run, integers have a size, values are copied or moved on purpose, and a failing function says so in its signature. This guide maps Python tasks to Bayan and explains the surprises; every output is real compiler output.</p>

